{
  "dom_id": "step-e7167",
  "name": "Example: Finding a Difference of Sets Using a Venn Diagram",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/96cd980d105fe04d2169f9252aa2e7e08bf57ba18cf7d7808d0c4c98c83f7767.png)\n\nGiven the sets $X = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ shown above, find $Y \\setminus X.$",
  "worked_solution": "The difference $Y \\setminus X$ consists of all the elements that are in $Y$ but not $X.$ To represent $Y \\setminus X,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $Y$ but not $X.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/5461edca3823f1cafd9f7b51528cd6eb1035e38f7f94c60177e369e2cdd5f350.png)\n\nThe only element in $Y$ that is not in $X$ is $4.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nY \\setminus X = \\{ 4 \\}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
